mac80211: minstrel_ht: respect the peer's Rx NSS

When a peer sends an Operating Mode Notification with fewer receive
streams, mac80211 lowers its rx_nss and asks rate control to update, but
minstrel_ht kept using every stream the capabilities allow. A STA shall
not transmit a frame with more spatial streams than the Rx NSS of the
most recent Operating Mode field received from the receiver (IEEE
802.11ac-2013 9.7.5.6).

Leave out HT and VHT groups with more streams than rx_nss.

--- a/net/mac80211/rc80211_minstrel_ht.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/rc80211_minstrel_ht.c
@@ -1800,6 +1800,10 @@ minstrel_ht_update_caps(void *priv, stru
 		if (sta->deflink.smps_mode == IEEE80211_SMPS_STATIC && nss > 1)
 			continue;
 
+		/* nor more streams than the peer receives, e.g. after an OMN */
+		if (sta->deflink.rx_nss && nss > sta->deflink.rx_nss)
+			continue;
+
 		/* HT rate */
 		if (gflags & IEEE80211_TX_RC_MCS) {
 			if (use_vht && minstrel_vht_only)
